	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1


                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILE:    PAGE.MAC
                                ; PROJECT: VI
                                ; MODULE:  WordMaster's file-I/O layer, transcribed VERBATIM from WM.ASM.
                                ;
                                ; This is the disk side of WordMaster's single-buffer design: the random-
                                ; record engine, the file primitives (open/close/make/rename/delete), and the
                                ; load (FILLBUF) and save (SAVCLO/FLUSHTX) drivers.  WordMaster's control flow
                                ; and instruction sequence are reproduced exactly (same assembled object code);
                                ; only the label NAMES are translated -- WM.ASM's address-derived labels (Lxxxx)
                                ; are renamed descriptively, which changes nothing in the assembled bytes.
                                ; Every routine cites its WM.ASM source line, so it still diffs against WM.ASM.
                                ;
                                ; WHAT IS HERE: the load path is FILLBUF and the save path SAVCLO/FLUSHTX --
                                ; the read and write sides of WordMaster's pager.  The window slides along a
                                ; file bigger than RAM through the eviction seam: MKROOM (SPILL forward, SPILLB
                                ; backward), REWIND, PAGEBOT, PAGEDIR/PAGEWIN/PGNEED and NEEDIN.  UPDMARK keeps
                                ; the three record marks (OUTREC/SRCREC/BAKREC) that let PAGEOUT and PAGEBOT
                                ; tell "already on disk" from "must transfer", so nothing is written twice or
                                ; lost; every mark starts each file at zero, as WM's per-file work-variable
                                ; clear leaves it.
                                ;
                                ; DEVIATIONS FROM WM (each is also flagged where it is):
                                ;   1. GETKEY -> KBPOLL.  RDSEC and POLLBRK drain type-ahead through WM's
                                ;      GETKEY; the ring is KEY.MAC's, so they call its KBPOLL.  POLLBRK keeps
                                ;      only WM's non-interruptible path (no ^C 'INTERRUPTED').  Harnesses
                                ;      without KEY.MAC supply a KBPOLL RET stub.
                                ;   2. FATAL -> JMP ERRMSG.  WM's FATAL (WM 5429) prints via CRLF/PUTSTR/CONOUT
                                ;      then JMP ABORT (screen + stack-unwind, neither exists).  It shares the
                                ;      'CALL x / DB msg,0' convention with ERRMSG, so FATAL just enters ERRMSG's
                                ;      tail (print msg, set ERRFLG, warm-boot).  Only reached on a disk error.
                                ;   3. OPENFIL / SAVEFIL wrappers.  WM's file-open is inline INIT code (WM
                                ;      412-519) and its save is ENDEDIT reached from the command loop (557-567);
                                ;      neither is a CALLable unit.  These two entry points run WM's exact
                                ;      instruction sequences verbatim, with the source FCB pre-staged at 005CH
                                ;      by CP/M from the command tail.  Same-drive / user-0 only: the multi-drive
                                ;      DRVMAP / DSTDRV branches (INIT 458-493) are omitted -- the bodies kept
                                ;      are verbatim.  A write to another drive is WRTO's, below.
                                ;   4. FILLBUF stores the last record's byte count (80H) for a full record with
                                ;      no ^Z, which WM does not -- WM's end-of-file bug; see FILLBUF.
                                ;   5. DISCRD skips the work-file deletes when this session never wrote a work
                                ;      record; see DISCRD.
                                ;   6. The backup work file is VIBACKUP.$$$, where WM names it WMBACKUP.$$$
                                ;      (BAKNAM).  Same length, so no layout moves.
                                ;   7. MEMSHT calls BUF.MAC's MEMERR, not ERRMSG: running out of room ends
                                ;      the key and leaves the editor up, as WM's prompt is left up (issue
                                ;      #39; BUF.MAC's deviation 3).
                                ;   8. The unchanged front (issue #34, part A).  SAMREC counts the records at
                                ;      the front of the file that are still the source's own: FFFFH at every
                                ;      open, lowered by UPDMARK beside OUTREC.  PAGEOUT does not write such a
                                ;      record (it raises OUTREC past it instead), REWIND reads it back from the
                                ;      source through a second FCB, SRCFCB, and SAVCLO copies them into
                                ;      name.$$$ first (SVFRNT), then writes the ones the save passes from RAM
                                ;      (SAVMOD).  So moving through a file writes nothing until it is edited,
                                ;      and only from the first edit on.  See PAGEOUT, REWIND, SAVCLO.
                                ;   9. WRREC keeps the record number when it makes the work file.  WM's
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-1


                                ;      DELRST zeroes it, which is harmless while the first write is always
                                ;      record 0; with deviation 8 the first can be any record.
                                ;
                                ; APPENDED (not WM), tagged where each starts: REOPEN/SEEKTO/OPENZ (':w' keeps
                                ; editing), TFCB/WRTO/TEXIST/DISCRD/CNTLF (':w name', ':e', a buffer with no
                                ; name), PGTOPM (the count of times the pager moved TXTBEG) and TOPLF with
                                ; TLFADD/TLFSUB (the line feeds behind the window, kept in PAGEOUT and REWIND).
                                ;============================================================
                                
  0000                          WBOOT	EQU	0
  0005                          BDOS	EQU	5
  001A                          EOF	EQU	1AH		; ^Z
  0008                          BS	EQU	08H
  0200                          PGINIT	EQU	200H		; WM 20 -- cold WRLIM/RDLIM (no-spill window)
                                
                                ;--- entry points the harness / editor calls -------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	OPENFIL
                                	PUBLIC	RENAME, BAKEXT	; PSV.MAC -- the pager tests' SAVEFIL
                                	PUBLIC	FILLBUF, SAVCLO
                                ;--- the disk seam BUF.MAC reaches -----------------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	MKROOM, REWIND, UPDMARK, MARKGB
                                ;--- scroll/search paging drivers (BUF.MAC's PAGESTP / SCRLST reach them)
                                	PUBLIC	PAGEDIR, PAGEWIN
                                	PUBLIC	POLLBRK		; break poll (CNTTST tail-calls it)
                                	PUBLIC	MOREIN		; WM 4743 -- GOLINE (BUF.MAC) tests it
                                ;--- data the harness reads to check state ---------------------------------
                                	PUBLIC	INRDY		; NZ while input remains (harness scroll loop)
                                ;--- on-demand page-in (BUF.MAC RGET) and the renderer's spill guard ------------
                                	PUBLIC	NEEDIN		; WM 4617 -- RGET pages input in
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi :w keeps editing (WM 'H' on the same file) ---
                                	PUBLIC	REOPEN, SEEKTO, OPENZ
                                ;--- APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi :w name, :e, a buffer with no name ---------
                                	PUBLIC	WRTO, TEXIST, DISCRD, CNTLF
                                	EXTRN	BINIT		; BUF.MAC -- WM L02F2 gap-pointer reset
                                	EXTRN	WRTYP, SECBUF	; RSV.MAC -- held above the image (see RSV.MAC)
                                
                                ;--- gap-buffer primitives + cells this layer drives (from BUF.MAC) ---------
                                	EXTRN	MEMCPY, CMP16, LDHLI, PRSPAN, BUFSUM
                                	EXTRN	PUTHOLE, PUTCUR, SUBHD, SUBCP2, POPRET, ERRMSG, MEMERR
                                	EXTRN	TXTBEG, GAPBEG, GAPEND, TXTEND, BUFEND
                                	EXTRN	KBPOLL		; KEY.MAC -- WM GETKEY (type-ahead drain)
                                
  0000'                         	CSEG
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; OPENFIL -- open the source file (staged at 005CH by CP/M) and read it into
                                ; the gap buffer.  Verbatim INIT subset (WM 412-518) + CMDINI limits (854);
                                ; wrapper glue only (deviation 3).  BINIT must have run first.
                                ;============================================================
  0000'                         OPENFIL:
  0000'   21 0200               	LXI	H,PGINIT	; WM 854 (CMDINI) -- no-spill window
  0003'   22 0000*              	SHLD	WRLIM
  0006'   22 0000*              	SHLD	RDLIM
  0009'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFEND		; WM 388/412 -- H = high byte of BUFEND
  000C'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  000D'   CD 023A'              	CALL	PGCONST		; paging constants (BUFHI/BUFLO/IOBATCH/...)
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-2


  0010'   21 005C               	LXI	H,5CH		; build OUTFCB as a copy of the source FCB
  0013'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0016'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  0019'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		; WM 462-463 -- 16-byte FCB header copy
  001C'   21 0946'              	LXI	H,BAKTYP	; set OUTFCB type = '$$$'  (WM 516-517)
  001F'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP
  0022'   CD 0821'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  0025'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	; zero OUTFCB random-record bytes
  0028'   CD 0789'              	CALL	ZERORR
  002B'   3A 005C               	LDA	5CH		; build BAKFCB = drive + 'VIBACKUP$$$'
  002E'   32 0000*              	STA	BAKFCB		; WM 479-485
  0031'   21 093E'              	LXI	H,BAKNAM
  0034'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0037'   13                    	INX	D
  0038'   01 000B               	LXI	B,0BH
  003B'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  003E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	; delete any stale name.$$$  (WM 513-514)
  0041'   CD 07B8'              	CALL	DELF
  0044'   21 0949'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT	; delete any stale name.BAK  (WM 510-517):
  0047'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP	;   point OUTTYP at 'BAK', delete, restore '$$$'
  004A'   CD 0821'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  004D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0050'   CD 07B8'              	CALL	DELF
  0053'   21 0946'              	LXI	H,BAKTYP
  0056'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTTYP
  0059'   CD 0821'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  005C'   11 005C               	LXI	D,5CH		; open the source file  (WM 496-505)
  005F'   CD 0784'              	CALL	OPENF
  0062'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  0064'   CA 0085'              	JZ	OPNEW
  0067'   32 005B               	STA	5BH		; source has data (input side live)
  006A'   21 005C               	LXI	H,5CH		; DEVIATION 8: SRCFCB is the source FCB as the
  006D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCFCB	;   open left it, so reading the records above
  0070'   01 0020               	LXI	B,20H		;   the window back costs no directory search.
  0073'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		;   CP/M 2.2 keeps nothing of an open file
  0076'   21 0020*              	LXI	H,SRCFCB+20H	;   outside its FCB.  Record, and the 'written'
  0079'   06 04                 	MVI	B,4H		;   byte SETREC reads, start at zero.
  007B'   36 00                 OPSZ:	MVI	M,0H
  007D'   23                    	INX	H
  007E'   05                    	DCR	B
  007F'   C2 007B'              	JNZ	OPSZ
  0082'   C3 0088'              	JMP	OPRD
  0085'                         OPNEW:				; source not found -> new file
  0085'   32 0000*              	STA	NEWFIL
  0088'                         OPRD:				; cold-start the pager state.  WM does this by
  0088'   AF                    	XRA	A		;   zeroing its whole work-variable area (WM
  0089'   32 0000*              	STA	BAKRDY		;   369-373, the L0307 clear loop over TXTROWS..
  008C'   32 0000*              	STA	OUTACT		 ;   2730): every deque mark -- OUTACT/OUTPOS/BAKPOS/
  008F'   32 0000*              	STA	INLEN		;   INLEN/OUTREC/SRCREC/BAKREC -- lives in that
  0092'   32 0000*              	STA	DIRFLG		;   region, so its true cold value is ZERO.  With
  0095'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD		; (deviation 8) not saving
  0098'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H		;   the real UPDMARK maintaining them (below), no
  009B'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC		;   bias is needed: at cold OUTPOS=0 and UPDMARK
  009E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRCREC		;   lowers it on an edit; PAGEOUT raises it.
  00A1'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  00A4'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKPOS
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-3


  00A7'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  00AA'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTHI		; (appended) name.$$$ holds no record yet
  00AD'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TOPLF		; (appended) no line is behind the window yet
  00B0'   2B                    	DCX	H		; DEVIATION 8: the source holds all of it
  00B1'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SAMREC
  00B4'   CD 03B2'              	CALL	FILLBUF		; WM 518 -- read the file into the buffer
  00B7'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi ':w' saves and keeps editing.  WM has no such
                                ; command -- its 'H' (EDNEXT, WM 525-545) ends the edit and re-inits for the
                                ; next file.  REOPEN is that re-init applied to the same file, and SEEKTO
                                ; pages the saved text back in up to the cursor's old place, flushing and
                                ; refilling exactly as the save loop (SAVCLO) does.  Without this, the editor
                                ; kept running on the flushed buffer and closed/renamed FCBs after a ':w'.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;REOPEN -- after a save: re-open the file named at 005CH and load its start.
  00B8'                         REOPEN:
  00B8'   CD 0795'              	CALL	CLSBAK		; WM 526 (EDNEXT)
  00BB'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BINIT		; WM L02F2 -- reset the gap pointers
                                ;OPENZ -- OPENFIL after WM's L02F2 clears (WM 369-376): the source FCB's input
                                ; flag, extent, record count and random record, and NEWFIL.  At start-up the
                                ; input flag (005BH) holds whatever the last program left there; a file that
                                ; is not found must not be read from.
  00BE'                         OPENZ:
  00BE'   AF                    	XRA	A
  00BF'   32 005B               	STA	5BH
  00C2'   32 0068               	STA	68H
  00C5'   32 006B               	STA	6BH
  00C8'   32 007D               	STA	7DH
  00CB'   32 0000*              	STA	NEWFIL
  00CE'   C3 0000'              	JMP	OPENFIL		; WM INIT: FCBs, stale-file deletes, open, fill
                                
                                ;SEEKTO -- DE = record, A = byte (0-127) of a file position: page forward
                                ;until that position is in the window.  HL = its logical offset (the end of
                                ;the text if the file is shorter).  OUTPOS*128 is TXTBEG's file position.
  00D1'                         SEEKTO:
  00D1'   32 0000*              	STA	SKBYT
  00D4'   EB                    	XCHG
  00D5'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SKREC
  00D8'                         SKLP:
  00D8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  00DB'   EB                    	XCHG
  00DC'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SKREC
  00DF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = records past TXTBEG's
  00E2'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  00E3'   FE 02                 	CPI	2H
  00E5'   D2 0106'              	JNC	SKMORE		; >= 200H records: not in the window
  00E8'   1F                    	RAR			; CY = bit 8 (H is 0 or 1)
  00E9'   7D                    	MOV	A,L
  00EA'   1F                    	RAR			; A = bits 8-1, CY = bit 0
  00EB'   57                    	MOV	D,A
  00EC'   3E 00                 	MVI	A,0
  00EE'   1F                    	RAR			; A = bit 0 << 7
  00EF'   5F                    	MOV	E,A
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-4


  00F0'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SKBYT
  00F3'   B3                    	ORA	E
  00F4'   5F                    	MOV	E,A		; DE = HL*128 + byte: the target offset
  00F5'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  00F6'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  00F9'   EB                    	XCHG
  00FA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  00FD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0100'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = text in the window
  0101'   E1                    	POP	H		; HL = target
  0102'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff length < target
  0105'   D0                    	RNC			; in the window
  0106'                         SKMORE:
  0106'   CD 0332'              	CALL	FLUSHTX		; WM 4850 (SAVCLO): write it all, refill
  0109'   CD 0398'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  010C'   D2 00D8'              	JNC	SKLP
  010F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG		; no more input: the end of the text
  0112'   EB                    	XCHG
  0113'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0116'   C3 0000*              	JMP	SUBHD
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; APPENDED (NOT WordMaster): vi writes the text to a name of its own (:w name,
                                ; and a buffer that has no name) and drops it for another file (:e).  WM always
                                ; writes back to the file it read.  These use WM's own primitives: SAVCLO for
                                ; the flush, RENAME for the backup, RENF, DELF, MAKEF, OPENF, CLOSEF.
                                ; TFCB holds the target name; the vi layer fills its drive, name and type
                                ; (bytes 0-11) and zeroes the rest.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;TEXIST -- Z iff no file has TFCB's name.
  0119'                         TEXIST:
  0119'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  011C'   CD 076A'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  011F'   11                    	DB	11H		; search for the first match
  0120'   3C                    	INR	A
  0121'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;WRTO -- write the whole text to the file named in TFCB (the edit is flushed
                                ; to name.$$$, as WM's ENDEDIT does).  A <> 0: a file already there becomes
                                ; name.BAK (WM ENDEDIT); A = 0: it is deleted (vim overwrites it).  Then
                                ; name.$$$ takes TFCB's name, by RENF on its own drive or by a copy to another
                                ; drive.  REOPEN must follow (from TFCB's name).
  0122'                         WRTO:
  0122'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  0123'   CD 0489'              	CALL	SAVCLO		; WM 558 (ENDEDIT)
  0126'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  0129'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  012A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  012B'   CA 0158'              	JZ	WRDEL
  012E'   21 0009*              	LXI	H,TFCB+9	; delete any old name.BAK
  0131'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,WRTYP
  0134'   CD 0821'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  0137'   11 0009*              	LXI	D,TFCB+9
  013A'   CD 081E'              	CALL	CPYBAK
  013D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-5


  0140'   CD 07B8'              	CALL	DELF
  0143'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,WRTYP
  0146'   11 0009*              	LXI	D,TFCB+9
  0149'   CD 0821'              	CALL	CPYTYP
  014C'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB		; name -> name.BAK (WM 562)
  014F'   21 0949'              	LXI	H,BAKEXT
  0152'   CD 07E2'              	CALL	RENAME
  0155'   C3 015B'              	JMP	WRMOV
  0158'                         WRDEL:
  0158'   CD 07B8'              	CALL	DELF
  015B'                         WRMOV:
  015B'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTFCB
  015E'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TFCB
  0161'   BE                    	CMP	M
  0162'   C2 0187'              	JNZ	WRCPY		; another drive
  0165'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,OUTFCB	; RENF block: name.$$$, then TFCB's name
  0168'   11 0010*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB+10H
  016B'   01 0010               	LXI	B,10H
  016E'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  0171'   21 0001*              	LXI	H,TFCB+1
  0174'   11 0011*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB+11H
  0177'   01 000B               	LXI	B,0BH
  017A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  017D'   AF                    	XRA	A
  017E'   32 0010*              	STA	OUTFCB+10H	; the new name's drive byte is 0 (as RENAME)
  0181'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0184'   C3 0801'              	JMP	RENF		; WM 566
  0187'                         WRCPY:				; name.$$$ copied record by record
  0187'   AF                    	XRA	A		; extent 0, record 0 on both
  0188'   32 000C*              	STA	OUTFCB+0CH
  018B'   32 0020*              	STA	OUTFCB+20H
  018E'   32 0020*              	STA	TFCB+20H
  0191'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0194'   CD 0784'              	CALL	OPENF
  0197'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  019A'   CD 07C4'              	CALL	DELRST		; make the new file
  019D'                         WRCLP:
  019D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  01A0'   CD 076A'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  01A3'   14                    	DB	14H		; read the next record
  01A4'   B7                    	ORA	A
  01A5'   C2 01B6'              	JNZ	WRCEND
  01A8'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  01AB'   CD 076A'              	CALL	BDOSFN
  01AE'   15                    	DB	15H		; write it
  01AF'   B7                    	ORA	A
  01B0'   CA 019D'              	JZ	WRCLP
  01B3'   C3 0880'              	JMP	DSKERR
  01B6'                         WRCEND:
  01B6'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TFCB
  01B9'   CD 079F'              	CALL	CLOSEF
  01BC'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  01BF'   C3 07B8'              	JMP	DELF
                                
                                ;DISCRD -- drop the edit: delete name.$$$ and VIBACKUP$$$ (WM EDEND, 581).
                                ;DEVIATION (not WordMaster): both are skipped when this session never wrote a
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-6


                                ;work record at all (WRKMAD clear), because then neither file can exist.  A BDOS
                                ;delete scans the whole directory whether or not the name is on it -- the best
                                ;part of a second each on a large drive -- and ':q' on a text that never spilled
                                ;paid it twice for nothing.  The per-file [FCB-2]/[FCB-1] flags will NOT do:
                                ;reading the backup back to its end clears them while the file is still there,
                                ;which is why WM's EDEND deletes unconditionally.
  01C2'                         DISCRD:
  01C2'   3A 0000*              	LDA	WRKMAD
  01C5'   B7                    	ORA	A
  01C6'   C8                    	RZ			; no work file was ever made: nothing to drop
  01C7'   AF                    	XRA	A
  01C8'   32 0000*              	STA	WRKMAD		; the deletes below leave nothing to drop again
  01CB'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  01CE'   CD 07B8'              	CALL	DELF
  01D1'   C3 07B2'              	JMP	KILLBAK
                                
                                ;CNTLF -- HL = the line feeds before the cursor: TOPLF for the records behind
                                ;the window, plus a scan of the text from TXTBEG to the gap.  It reads no disk.
  01D4'                         CNTLF:
  01D4'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  01D7'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CLCNT
  01DA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  01DD'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  01DE'   EB                    	XCHG
  01DF'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  01E2'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  01E5'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the text before the gap
  01E6'   E1                    	POP	H
  01E7'   CD 0223'              	CALL	CLBYTS
  01EA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CLCNT
  01ED'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;TLFADD / TLFSUB -- the sector at HL leaves the window's top (PAGEOUT) or comes
                                ;back to it (REWIND): TOPLF gains or loses its line feeds.  TOPLF is then the
                                ;line feeds in output records 0 to OUTPOS-1 at all times, which is what CNTLF
                                ;used to read those records back to find.  Keeps every register and the flags.
  01EE'                         TLFADD:
  01EE'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  01EF'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  01F0'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  01F1'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  01F2'   CD 0211'              	CALL	TLFSEC
  01F5'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  01F8'   19                    	DAD	D
  01F9'   C3 0209'              	JMP	TLFSTO
  01FC'                         TLFSUB:
  01FC'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  01FD'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  01FE'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  01FF'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0200'   CD 0211'              	CALL	TLFSEC
  0203'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TOPLF
  0206'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0209'                         TLFSTO:
  0209'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TOPLF
  020C'   E1                    	POP	H
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-7


  020D'   D1                    	POP	D
  020E'   C1                    	POP	B
  020F'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  0210'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;TLFSEC -- DE = the line feeds in the 128 bytes at HL.
  0211'                         TLFSEC:
  0211'   11 0000               	LXI	D,0
  0214'   06 80                 	MVI	B,80H
  0216'                         TLFLP:
  0216'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  0217'   23                    	INX	H
  0218'   FE 0A                 	CPI	0AH
  021A'   C2 021E'              	JNZ	TLFNX
  021D'   13                    	INX	D
  021E'                         TLFNX:
  021E'   05                    	DCR	B
  021F'   C2 0216'              	JNZ	TLFLP
  0222'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLBYTS -- HL = text, DE = its length: CLCNT += its line feeds.
  0223'                         CLBYTS:
  0223'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  0224'   B3                    	ORA	E
  0225'   C8                    	RZ
  0226'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  0227'   23                    	INX	H
  0228'   1B                    	DCX	D
  0229'   FE 0A                 	CPI	0AH
  022B'   C2 0223'              	JNZ	CLBYTS
  022E'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  022F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CLCNT
  0232'   23                    	INX	H
  0233'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CLCNT
  0236'   E1                    	POP	H
  0237'   C3 0223'              	JMP	CLBYTS
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; PAGING CONSTANTS -- WM 412-447.  From A/H = high byte of BUFEND, derive the
                                ; batch/margin sizing and the free-space water marks the load/spill path reads.
                                ;============================================================
  023A'                         PGCONST:			; WM 412
  023A'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  023B'   B7                    	ORA	A
  023C'   1F                    	RAR
  023D'   1F                    	RAR
  023E'   1F                    	RAR
  023F'   3C                    	INR	A
  0240'   3C                    	INR	A
  0241'   E6 3C                 	ANI	3CH
  0243'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  0244'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCAL
  0247'   07                    	RLC
  0248'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCL2
  024B'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  024C'   FE 08                 	CPI	BS
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-8


  024E'   D2 0253'              	JNC	PGCON1
  0251'   3E 08                 	MVI	A,BS
  0253'                         PGCON1:				 ; WM 430
  0253'   32 0000*              	STA	PGMARGN
  0256'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  0257'   FE 64                 	CPI	64H
  0259'   21 0400               	LXI	H,400H
  025C'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BUFLO
  025F'   DA 0263'              	JC	PGCON2
  0262'   29                    	DAD	H
  0263'                         PGCON2:				 ; WM 439
  0263'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BUFHI
  0266'   3E 08                 	MVI	A,BS
  0268'   32 0000*              	STA	PGSCRA
  026B'   DA 026F'              	JC	PGCON3
  026E'   87                    	ADD	A
  026F'                         PGCON3:				 ; WM 446
  026F'   32 0000*              	STA	IOBATCH
  0272'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SPILL / PAGEOUT / FLUSHTX -- the output (write-behind) side.  RAM-only, SPILL
                                ; no-ops (CKWRLIM) on load and FLUSHTX drains the whole buffer on save.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;SPILL -- WM 4386: write-behind a batch of TXTBEG-side sectors to OUTFCB.
  0273'                         SPILL:				; WM 4386
  0273'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0274'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0275'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0276'   CD 02A2'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  0279'   DA 0000*              	JC	POPRET
  027C'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SPLCNT
  027F'   34                    	INR	M
  0280'   46                    	MOV	B,M
  0281'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,PGSCL2
  0284'   AF                    	XRA	A
  0285'                         SPLSUM:				 ; WM 4398
  0285'   86                    	ADD	M
  0286'   05                    	DCR	B
  0287'   C2 0285'              	JNZ	SPLSUM
  028A'   3D                    	DCR	A
  028B'   F6 07                 	ORI	7H
  028D'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  028E'   3A 0000*              	LDA	IOBATCH
  0291'   3D                    	DCR	A
  0292'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  0293'                         SPLLP:				; WM 4409
  0293'   CD 02A2'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  0296'   05                    	DCR	B
  0297'   CA 029E'              	JZ	SPLDON
  029A'   0D                    	DCR	C
  029B'   C2 0293'              	JNZ	SPLLP
  029E'                         SPLDON:				 ; WM 4416
  029E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  029F'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-9


                                
                                ;PAGEOUT -- WM 4439: spill one sector at TXTBEG to OUTFCB, bump TXTBEG.
                                ;DEVIATION 8: a record below SAMREC is the source's own and is not written;
                                ;OUTREC rises past it, so OUTREC still equals OUTPOS at every fresh write
                                ;(POFRSH adds one to OUTREC, not to OUTPOS).  OUTREC then means "valid in
                                ;name.$$$ or in the source".  While SAVCLO saves (SAVMOD), such a record IS
                                ;written, from RAM, and OUTREC is left alone.
  02A2'                         PAGEOUT:			; WM 4439
  02A2'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  02A5'   CD 057C'              	CALL	CKWRLIM
  02A8'   D8                    	RC
  02A9'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  02AA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  02AD'   EB                    	XCHG
  02AE'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; DEVIATION 8
  02B1'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  02B4'   DA 02FD'              	JC	POSAME
  02B7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  02BA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  02BD'   E1                    	POP	H
  02BE'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  02C1'   D2 02CA'              	JNC	POFRSH
  02C4'   CD 08B9'              	CALL	RECINC
  02C7'   C3 02E9'              	JMP	POADV
  02CA'                         POFRSH:				 ; WM 4454 -- write a fresh output record
  02CA'   CD 08B3'              	CALL	WRRECP
  02CD'   EB                    	XCHG
  02CE'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  02D1'   23                    	INX	H
  02D2'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC
  02D5'   D5                    POWHI:	PUSH	D		; (appended) OUTHI follows the most records
  02D6'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTHI		;   name.$$$ has ever held; OUTREC cannot
  02D9'   EB                    	XCHG			;   say, an edit behind it brings it down
  02DA'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  02DD'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  02E0'   D2 02E6'              	JNC	POHI
  02E3'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTHI
  02E6'   D1                    POHI:	POP	D
  02E7'   EB                    	XCHG
  02E8'   04                    	INR	B
  02E9'                         POADV:				; WM 4463 -- advance TXTBEG past the sector
  02E9'   CD 01EE'              	CALL	TLFADD		; (appended) its line feeds are behind the
                                				;   window now
  02EC'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  02EF'   19                    	DAD	D
  02F0'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTBEG
  02F3'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  02F4'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; (appended) the window's top moved: 'u' reads
  02F7'   23                    	INX	H		;   this to know its offsets have shifted
  02F8'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  02FB'   E1                    	POP	H
  02FC'   C9                    	RET
  02FD'                         POSAME:				; DEVIATION 8: the source holds this record
  02FD'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SAVMOD
  0300'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0301'   C2 0327'              	JNZ	POSAVE
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-10


  0304'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  0307'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < OUTREC: counted already, as
  030A'   DA 031D'              	JC	POSAM1		;   WM skips a record already written
  030D'   13                    	INX	D
  030E'   EB                    	XCHG
  030F'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC		; OUTREC = OUTPOS+1
  0312'   E1                    	POP	H
  0313'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0316'   CD 08B9'              	CALL	RECINC		; past it, unwritten -- and where WM would have
  0319'   04                    	INR	B		;   written it, SPILL's batch counts it as WM's
  031A'   C3 02E9'              	JMP	POADV		;   does, so a first pass empties the window
  031D'   E1                    POSAM1:	POP	H
  031E'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0321'   CD 08B9'              	CALL	RECINC
  0324'   C3 02E9'              	JMP	POADV
  0327'   E1                    POSAVE:	POP	H		; saving: write it from RAM
  0328'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  032B'   CD 08B3'              	CALL	WRRECP
  032E'   EB                    	XCHG
  032F'   C3 02D5'              	JMP	POWHI
                                
                                ;FLUSHTX -- WM 4471: collapse the gap and PAGEOUT every remaining sector.
  0332'                         FLUSHTX:			; WM 4471
  0332'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0333'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0334'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0335'   21 0081               	LXI	H,81H
  0338'   22 0000*              	SHLD	WRLIM
  033B'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  033E'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE
  0341'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0344'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTCUR
  0347'                         FLXLP:				; WM 4482 -- flush loop
  0347'   CD 02A2'              	CALL	PAGEOUT
  034A'   D2 0347'              	JNC	FLXLP
  034D'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;STAGSEC -- WM 4588: stage a short final record into SECBUF, ^Z-pad the tail.
  0350'                         STAGSEC:			; WM 4588
  0350'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0351'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0352'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  0355'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0356'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  0357'   0E 82                 	MVI	C,82H
  0359'   04                    	INR	B
  035A'   2B                    	DCX	H
  035B'   1B                    	DCX	D
  035C'                         STGCPY:				 ; WM 4599 -- copy the partial sector
  035C'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  035D'   12                    	STAX	D
  035E'   23                    	INX	H
  035F'   13                    	INX	D
  0360'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0361'   05                    	DCR	B
  0362'   C2 035C'              	JNZ	STGCPY
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-11


  0365'                         STGPAD:				 ; WM 4608 -- pad the rest with ^Z
  0365'   3E 1A                 	MVI	A,EOF
  0367'   12                    	STAX	D
  0368'   13                    	INX	D
  0369'   0D                    	DCR	C
  036A'   C2 0365'              	JNZ	STGPAD
  036D'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FILLBUF / RDIN / CLNSEC -- the input (read) side.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;NEEDIN -- WM 4617: page input in when the forward read (RGET) runs dry.
                                ;SPILL first if free space is under a record, then reserve and fill.
  0370'                         NEEDIN:				; WM 4617
  0370'   CD 0413'              	CALL	INRDY
  0373'   C8                    	RZ
  0374'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0375'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0376'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0377'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  037A'   21 0080               	LXI	H,80H
  037D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0380'   EB                    	XCHG
  0381'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFHI
  0384'   D2 038E'              	JNC	NDIRSV
  0387'   CD 0273'              	CALL	SPILL
  038A'   DA 0451'              	JC	MEMSHT
  038D'   EB                    	XCHG
  038E'                         NDIRSV:				 ; WM 4633 -- reserve free space, then fill
  038E'   EB                    	XCHG
  038F'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  0392'   CD 0444'              	CALL	FREEREC
  0395'   C3 03C1'              	JMP	FILLRD
                                
                                ;FILLBF2 -- WM 4640: fill from input, capped at 7800H.
  0398'                         FILLBF2:			; WM 4640
  0398'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0399'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  039A'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  039B'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  039E'   11 7800               	LXI	D,7800H
  03A1'   CD 0475'              	CALL	BUFFREE
  03A4'   CD 0413'              	CALL	INRDY
  03A7'   CA 03DC'              	JZ	FILRET
  03AA'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  03AB'   B7                    	ORA	A
  03AC'   C2 03C1'              	JNZ	FILLRD
  03AF'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;FILLBUF -- WM 4659: top the window up from the input file(s).
  03B2'                         FILLBUF:			; WM 4659
  03B2'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  03B3'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  03B4'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  03B5'   CD 0413'              	CALL	INRDY
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-12


  03B8'   CA 03DC'              	JZ	FILRET
  03BB'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND
  03BE'   CD 042A'              	CALL	RESVBF0
  03C1'                         FILLRD:				 ; WM 4668
  03C1'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  03C4'                         FILRLP:				 ; WM 4671 -- read & clean one input record
  03C4'   CD 03DF'              	CALL	RDIN
  03C7'   D4 03F8'              	CNC	CLNSEC
  03CA'   D2 03D1'              	JNC	FILRSV		; DEVIATION (WM bug): WM is JC L1C6B, which
  03CD'   B7                    	ORA	A		;   skips the store for a full record (CY,
  03CE'   CA 03D4'              	JZ	FILRST		;   A=80H), so a file ending on a record
  03D1'   32 0000*              FILRSV: STA	INLEN		;   boundary w/o ^Z leaves INLEN=0 and PAGEBOT
                                				;   RECDECs one record too far (record saved
                                				;   twice).  Skip only RDIN's no-record case
                                				;   (CY, A=0).
  03D4'                         FILRST:				 ; WM 4677
  03D4'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  03D7'   0D                    	DCR	C
  03D8'   C2 03C4'              	JNZ	FILRLP
  03DB'   B7                    	ORA	A
  03DC'                         FILRET:				 ; WM 4683
  03DC'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RDIN -- WM 4689: read the next input record into [HL] (backup then source).
  03DF'                         RDIN:				; WM 4689
  03DF'   CD 0938'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  03E2'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKRDY
  03E5'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  03E6'   13                    	INX	D
  03E7'   B7                    	ORA	A
  03E8'   37                    	STC
  03E9'   C4 082E'              	CNZ	RDPREV
  03EC'   D0                    	RNC
  03ED'   11 005B               	LXI	D,5BH
  03F0'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  03F1'   13                    	INX	D
  03F2'   B7                    	ORA	A
  03F3'   37                    	STC
  03F4'   C4 0827'              	CNZ	RDNEXT
  03F7'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;CLNSEC -- WM 4709: mask bit 7, stop at ^Z; return live byte count in A.
  03F8'                         CLNSEC:				; WM 4709
  03F8'   06 80                 	MVI	B,80H
  03FA'                         CLNLP:				; WM 4712
  03FA'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  03FB'   E6 7F                 	ANI	7FH
  03FD'   77                    	MOV	M,A
  03FE'   FE 1A                 	CPI	EOF
  0400'   CA 040C'              	JZ	CLNEOF
  0403'   23                    	INX	H
  0404'   05                    	DCR	B
  0405'   C2 03FA'              	JNZ	CLNLP
  0408'   37                    	STC
  0409'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  040B'   C9                    	RET
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-13


  040C'                         CLNEOF:				 ; WM 4725 -- input EOF: return the byte count
  040C'   CD 0843'              	CALL	IOEOF
  040F'   3E 80                 	MVI	A,80H
  0411'   90                    	SUB	B
  0412'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;INRDY -- WM 4733: NZ while any input data is still unread.
  0413'                         INRDY:				; WM 4733
  0413'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0414'   3A 005B               	LDA	5BH
  0417'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BAKRDY
  041A'   B6                    	ORA	M
  041B'   37                    	STC
  041C'   E1                    	POP	H
  041D'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;MOREIN -- WM 4743: NZ if more input remains in the current direction
                                ;(WM's L26AA is OUTACT, the byte before OUTFCB).
  041E'                         MOREIN:				; WM 4743
  041E'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  0421'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0422'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTACT
  0425'   F4 0413'              	CP	INRDY
  0428'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0429'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; FREE-SPACE ACCOUNTING -- WM 4786-4841.  Reserve/compute the read-ahead room.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;RESVBF0/RESVBUF -- WM 4786/4790: reserve free buffer space up to BUFHI.
  042A'                         RESVBF0:			; WM 4786
  042A'   11 0273'              	LXI	D,SPILL
  042D'                         RESVBUF:			; WM 4790
  042D'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  042E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFHI
  0431'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0432'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  0435'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0438'   E1                    	POP	H
  0439'   DC 0474'              	CC	DISPKEY
  043C'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFLO
  043F'   29                    	DAD	H
  0440'   24                    	INR	H
  0441'   24                    	INR	H
  0442'   EB                    	XCHG
  0443'   E1                    	POP	H
  0444'                         FREEREC:			; WM 4806 -- free bytes -> capped record count
  0444'   CD 0475'              	CALL	BUFFREE
  0447'   FE 08                 	CPI	BS
  0449'   DA 044F'              	JC	FRECOK
  044C'   D6 04                 	SUI	4H
  044E'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  044F'                         FRECOK:				 ; WM 4813
  044F'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0450'   C0                    	RNZ
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-14


  0451'                         MEMSHT:				 ; WM 4817
  0451'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMERR		; DEVIATION 7: out of room ends the key, not
                                				;   the editor (BUF.MAC's deviation 3)
  0454'   4D 45 4D 20           	DB	'MEM SHORTAGE, TRY CLEARING QBUF',0H
  0458'   53 48 4F 52           
  045C'   54 41 47 45           
  0460'   2C 20 54 52           
  0464'   59 20 43 4C           
  0468'   45 41 52 49           
  046C'   4E 47 20 51           
  0470'   42 55 46 00           
                                
                                ;DISPKEY -- WM 2846: PCHL trampoline (call the reserve routine held in HL).
  0474'                         DISPKEY:			; WM 2846
  0474'   E9                    	PCHL
                                
                                ;BUFFREE -- WM 4827: collapse the gap and report free bytes (A/C = pages).
  0475'                         BUFFREE:			; WM 4827
  0475'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE
  0478'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0479'   CD 0000*              	CALL	BUFSUM
  047C'   E1                    	POP	H
  047D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBCP2
  0480'   EB                    	XCHG
  0481'   29                    	DAD	H
  0482'                         BFRLP:				; WM 4836
  0482'   DA 0482'              	JC	BFRLP
  0485'   EB                    	XCHG
  0486'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  0487'   4A                    	MOV	C,D
  0488'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SAVCLO -- WM 4846: flush all buffered text to OUTFCB and close it.
                                ;============================================================
  0489'                         SAVCLO:				; WM 4846
  0489'   CD 04CC'              	CALL	SVBEG		; DEVIATION 8: the source's front, counted
  048C'   CD 0398'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  048F'                         SAVLP:				; WM 4849 -- flush all, refill, repeat
  048F'   CD 0332'              	CALL	FLUSHTX
  0492'   CD 04E9'              	CALL	SVFRNT		; DEVIATION 8: ... and copied, the first time
  0495'   CD 0398'              	CALL	FILLBF2
  0498'   D2 048F'              	JNC	SAVLP
  049B'   AF                    	XRA	A		; DEVIATION 8: the pass is over
  049C'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD
  049F'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  04A2'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
  04A5'   CD 0000*              	CALL	LDHLI
  04A8'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  04A9'   CD 0350'              	CALL	STAGSEC
  04AC'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  04AF'   CD 08B3'              	CALL	WRRECP
  04B2'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS		; DEVIATION (not WM): WM closes here.  Text
  04B5'   EB                    	XCHG			;   that was paged out, rewound and then cut
  04B6'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTHI		;   short leaves the old records after the
  04B9'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		;   last one, and CP/M cannot drop them.  A
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-15


  04BC'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB	;   part-filled last record hides them behind
  04BF'   D2 079F'              	JNC	CLOSEF		;   its ^Z padding; a full one has none, and
  04C2'   AF                    	XRA	A		;   the old text was read back as the file's
  04C3'   CD 0350'              	CALL	STAGSEC		;   end.  So a record of ^Z goes over the
  04C6'   CD 08B3'              	CALL	WRRECP		;   first of them.  It is there already:
  04C9'   C3 079F'              	JMP	CLOSEF		;   this write cannot fill the disk.
                                
                                ;SVBEG / SVFRNT -- DEVIATION 8: the records above the window that the source
                                ;still holds (0 to the lower of SAMREC and OUTPOS) are not in name.$$$.  SVBEG
                                ;counts them as the save begins (SVFCNT) and sets SAVMOD, so the save writes
                                ;the other records below SAMREC from RAM as it passes them; the records from
                                ;SAMREC to OUTPOS are in name.$$$ already.  SVFRNT, after the save's first
                                ;FLUSHTX has emptied the window, copies them from the source, bit 7 cleared
                                ;as a load clears it, through the free RAM above TXTEND: as many as it holds
                                ;are read, then written.  One record at a time, read and write alternate,
                                ;and the BIOS's deblocking makes each call about ten times dearer (0.37 s a
                                ;read, measured on the simulator's 8 MB drive).  The free RAM is at least the
                                ;0D80H a full register leaves.  OUTPOS, the save's place, is put back.
  04CC'                         SVBEG:
  04CC'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  04CE'   32 0000*              	STA	SAVMOD
  04D1'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  04D4'   EB                    	XCHG
  04D5'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  04D8'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  04DB'   D2 04DF'              	JNC	SVBN
  04DE'   EB                    	XCHG
  04DF'   22 0000*              SVBN:	SHLD	SVFCNT
  04E2'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0H
  04E5'   22 0022*              	SHLD	SRCFCB+22H
  04E8'   C9                    	RET
  04E9'                         SVFRNT:
  04E9'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SVFCNT
  04EC'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  04ED'   B5                    	ORA	L
  04EE'   C8                    	RZ
  04EF'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  04F2'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  04F3'   2A 0022*              	LHLD	SRCFCB+22H	; the next record: OUTPOS keeps pace with it
  04F6'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  04F9'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,BUFEND	; all the free RAM above the text (FILLBF2's
  04FC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PUTHOLE		;   BUFFREE does the same next)
  04FF'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0502'   EB                    	XCHG
  0503'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BUFEND
  0506'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = the free bytes above the text
  0509'   29                    	DAD	H
  050A'   4C                    	MOV	C,H
  050B'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0H		; BC = the records they hold
  050D'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  050E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  050F'   C2 0522'              	JNZ	SVFFIT
  0512'   CD 0781'              	CALL	FATAL		; cannot happen (see above): stop, never loop
  0515'   4D 45 4D 20           	DB	'MEM SHORTAGE',0H
  0519'   53 48 4F 52           
  051D'   54 41 47 45           
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-16


  0521'   00                    
  0522'   2A 0000*              SVFFIT:	LHLD	SVFCNT
  0525'   50                    	MOV	D,B
  0526'   59                    	MOV	E,C
  0527'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff they hold fewer than are left
  052A'   DA 052F'              	JC	SVFN
  052D'   44                    	MOV	B,H
  052E'   4D                    	MOV	C,L		; BC = this batch
  052F'   50                    SVFN:	MOV	D,B
  0530'   59                    	MOV	E,C
  0531'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = what is left after it
  0534'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SVFCNT
  0537'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0538'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  053B'   11 0000*              SVFRD:	LXI	D,SRCFCB
  053E'   CD 0827'              	CALL	RDNEXT
  0541'   D2 0550'              	JNC	SVFOK
  0544'   CD 0781'              	CALL	FATAL		; the source ends early: never save half of it
  0547'   52 45 41 44           	DB	'READ ERR',0H
  054B'   20 45 52 52           
  054F'   00                    
  0550'   C5                    SVFOK:	PUSH	B
  0551'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0552'   CD 03F8'              	CALL	CLNSEC
  0555'   E1                    	POP	H
  0556'   C1                    	POP	B
  0557'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  055A'   19                    	DAD	D
  055B'   0B                    	DCX	B
  055C'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  055D'   B1                    	ORA	C
  055E'   C2 053B'              	JNZ	SVFRD
  0561'   C1                    	POP	B
  0562'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  0565'   11 0000*              SVFWR:	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0568'   CD 08B3'              	CALL	WRRECP
  056B'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  056E'   19                    	DAD	D
  056F'   0B                    	DCX	B
  0570'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  0571'   B1                    	ORA	C
  0572'   C2 0565'              	JNZ	SVFWR
  0575'   E1                    	POP	H
  0576'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTPOS
  0579'   C3 04E9'              	JMP	SVFRNT		; the next batch, if any
                                
                                ;CKWRLIM -- WM 4863: CY if GAPBEG is below the PAGEOUT write limit.
  057C'                         CKWRLIM:			; WM 4863
  057C'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  057D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	WRLIM
  0580'   EB                    	XCHG
  0581'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  0584'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0587'   EB                    	XCHG
  0588'   E1                    	POP	H
  0589'   C3 0000*              	JMP	CMP16
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-17


                                
                                ;CKRDLIM -- WM 4874: compare GAPEND against the read limit (PAGEBOT guard).
  058C'                         CKRDLIM:			; WM 4874
  058C'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  058D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	RDLIM
  0590'   EB                    	XCHG
  0591'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND
  0594'   19                    	DAD	D
  0595'   D1                    	POP	D
  0596'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0599'   EB                    	XCHG
  059A'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; EVICTION SEAM + DEQUE MARKS.  Transcribed VERBATIM (WM 4335-4962).
                                ; MKGAP (BUF.MAC) reaches disk only here: MKROOM evicts a window edge (SPILL the
                                ; TXTBEG side to OUTFCB when scrolling forward, SPILLB the TXTEND side back to
                                ; the input/backup side when scrolling back).  UPDMARK keeps the three record
                                ; marks (OUTREC / SRCREC / BAKREC) that let PAGEOUT and PAGEBOT tell "already on
                                ; disk" from "must transfer", so nothing is written twice or lost.
                                ; PAGEDIR / PAGEWIN / PGNEED (scroll- and search-time paging) are real below:
                                ; PAGEDIR picks REWIND (backward, re-read spilled text) vs FILLBUF (forward),
                                ; and PGNEED / PAGEWIN keep PGMARGN bytes of text resident on the active edge.
                                ; The editor reaches them through BUF.MAC's PAGESTP and SCRLST (the line moves,
                                ; the line kill and the search sweep); PGBKTST drives PAGEDIR directly.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;PAGEDIR -- WM 4320: page more text into the window in the current scroll
                                ;direction -- REWIND (re-read text previously spilled to OUTFCB) when DIRFLG is
                                ;backward, else FILLBUF (read more of the input) when forward.
  059B'                         PAGEDIR:			; WM 4320
  059B'   CD 0938'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  059E'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  05A1'   B7                    	ORA	A
  05A2'   FA 0674'              	JM	REWIND
  05A5'   C3 03B2'              	JMP	FILLBUF
                                
                                ;MKROOM -- WM 4335: free gap space by evicting a window edge (DIRFLG picks).
  05A8'                         MKROOM:				; WM 4335
  05A8'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  05AB'   B7                    	ORA	A
  05AC'   37                    	STC
  05AD'   FC 05E7'              	CM	SPILLB
  05B0'   D0                    	RNC
  05B1'   CD 0273'              	CALL	SPILL
  05B4'   D0                    	RNC
  05B5'   C3 05E7'              	JMP	SPILLB
                                
                                ;PAGEWIN -- WM 4350: keep PGMARGN bytes of text buffered around the cursor on
                                ;the active edge (for a whole-file search); PAGEDIR one increment at a time
                                ;until PGNEED is satisfied or the source runs out.
  05B8'                         PAGEWIN:			; WM 4350
  05B8'   CD 05C8'              	CALL	PGNEED
  05BB'   D8                    	RC
  05BC'   CD 059B'              	CALL	PAGEDIR
  05BF'   D8                    	RC
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-18


  05C0'   CD 05C8'              	CALL	PGNEED
  05C3'   D4 059B'              	CNC	PAGEDIR
  05C6'   B7                    	ORA	A
  05C7'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;PGNEED -- WM 4361: CY if the active edge (TXTBEG scanning back, GAPEND scanning
                                ;forward) is still within PGMARGN*256 bytes -- i.e. the resident text on that
                                ;side is shorter than the margin, so more must be paged in.  LHLD MARGLO reads
                                ;the word whose high byte is PGMARGN and whose low byte (MARGLO) is a fixed 0,
                                ;yielding PGMARGN*256 (WM does this as LHLD 272F).
  05C8'                         PGNEED:				; WM 4361
  05C8'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  05C9'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  05CA'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  05CB'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  05CE'   B7                    	ORA	A
  05CF'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,TXTBEG
  05D2'   FA 05D8'              	JM	PGNCMP
  05D5'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,GAPEND
  05D8'                         PGNCMP:				 ; WM 4371 -- span the active edge, compare to margin
  05D8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	MARGLO
  05DB'   EB                    	XCHG
  05DC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	PRSPAN
  05DF'   60                    	MOV	H,B
  05E0'   69                    	MOV	L,C
  05E1'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  05E4'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;SPILLB -- WM 4491: evict a batch of bottom (TXTEND-side) sectors via PAGEBOT.
  05E7'                         SPILLB:				; WM 4491
  05E7'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  05E8'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  05E9'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  05EA'   CD 0607'              	CALL	PAGEBOT
  05ED'   DA 0000*              	JC	POPRET
  05F0'   3A 0000*              	LDA	IOBATCH
  05F3'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  05F4'   05                    	DCR	B
  05F5'   87                    	ADD	A
  05F6'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  05F7'   0D                    	DCR	C
  05F8'                         SPBLP:				; WM 4504 -- evict-batch loop
  05F8'   CD 0607'              	CALL	PAGEBOT
  05FB'   05                    	DCR	B
  05FC'   CA 0603'              	JZ	SPBDON
  05FF'   0D                    	DCR	C
  0600'   C2 05F8'              	JNZ	SPBLP
  0603'                         SPBDON:				 ; WM 4511
  0603'   B7                    	ORA	A
  0604'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;PAGEBOT -- WM 4520: evict the window's bottom sector back to the input side.
                                ;If it still aligns with the original, un-read the source (RECDEC); otherwise
                                ;write it to VIBACKUP$$$ -- SRCREC/BAKREC decide which.  Then TXTEND -= 128.
  0607'                         PAGEBOT:			; WM 4520
  0607'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-19


  060A'   CD 0413'              	CALL	INRDY
  060D'   C2 061F'              	JNZ	PBSTEP
  0610'   3A 0000*              	LDA	INLEN
  0613'   57                    	MOV	D,A
  0614'   CD 075F'              	CALL	SUBHA
  0617'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0618'   7A                    	MOV	A,D
  0619'   CD 0350'              	CALL	STAGSEC
  061C'   C3 0624'              	JMP	PBRDLM
  061F'                         PBSTEP:				 ; WM 4532 -- step back one sector at TXTEND
  061F'   11 FF80               	LXI	D,0FF80H
  0622'   19                    	DAD	D
  0623'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0624'                         PBRDLM:				 ; WM 4537 -- check the read limit
  0624'   E3                    	XTHL
  0625'   CD 058C'              	CALL	CKRDLIM
  0628'   E3                    	XTHL
  0629'   D2 062E'              	JNC	PBSRC
  062C'   E1                    	POP	H
  062D'   C9                    	RET
  062E'                         PBSRC:				; WM 4545 -- read from the source if its rec is due
  062E'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  062F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRCREC
  0632'   EB                    	XCHG
  0633'   CD 0740'              	CALL	RECBASE
  0636'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0639'   E1                    	POP	H
  063A'   D2 0646'              	JNC	PBBAK
  063D'   11 005C               	LXI	D,5CH
  0640'   CD 08C0'              	CALL	RECDEC
  0643'   C3 066B'              	JMP	PBFIN
  0646'                         PBBAK:				; WM 4557 -- else read / recycle from the backup
  0646'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0647'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  064A'   EB                    	XCHG
  064B'   CD 0740'              	CALL	RECBASE
  064E'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0651'   E1                    	POP	H
  0652'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,BAKFCB
  0655'   D2 065E'              	JNC	PBWBAK
  0658'   CD 08B9'              	CALL	RECINC
  065B'   C3 066B'              	JMP	PBFIN
  065E'                         PBWBAK:				 ; WM 4569 -- write back a backup record; step BAKREC
  065E'   CD 08B3'              	CALL	WRRECP
  0661'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0662'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  0665'   2B                    	DCX	H
  0666'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  0669'   E1                    	POP	H
  066A'   04                    	INR	B
  066B'                         PBFIN:				; WM 4578 -- store new TXTEND; note input remaining
  066B'   CD 0413'              	CALL	INRDY
  066E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  066F'   E1                    	POP	H
  0670'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTEND
  0673'   C9                    	RET
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-20


                                
                                ;REWIND -- WM 4755: scrolling back, re-read sectors previously spilled to
                                ;OUTFCB (by random record, stepping backward) and prepend them at TXTBEG.
                                ;Enabled only when OUTACT marks that text has actually been written out.
  0674'                         REWIND:				; WM 4755
  0674'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  0675'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0676'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  0677'   3A 0000*              	LDA	OUTACT
  067A'   B7                    	ORA	A
  067B'   37                    	STC
  067C'   CA 06AF'              	JZ	RWNRET
  067F'   11 05E7'              	LXI	D,SPILLB
  0682'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  0685'   CD 042D'              	CALL	RESVBUF
  0688'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
  068B'                         RWNLP:				; WM 4768 -- re-read one output record backward
  068B'   CD 0938'              	CALL	POLLBRK
  068E'   11 FF80               	LXI	D,0FF80H
  0691'   19                    	DAD	D
  0692'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  0695'   CD 06B2'              	CALL	RWNREC		; DEVIATION 8: RDPREV, or from the source
  0698'   DA 06AE'              	JC	RWNDON
  069B'   22 0000*              	SHLD	TXTBEG
  069E'   CD 01FC'              	CALL	TLFSUB		; (appended) its line feeds are back in the
                                				;   window
  06A1'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06A2'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	PGTOPM		; (appended) the window's top moved: 'u' reads
  06A5'   23                    	INX	H		;   this to know its offsets have shifted
  06A6'   22 0000*              	SHLD	PGTOPM
  06A9'   E1                    	POP	H
  06AA'   0D                    	DCR	C
  06AB'   C2 068B'              	JNZ	RWNLP
  06AE'                         RWNDON:				 ; WM 4779
  06AE'   B7                    	ORA	A
  06AF'                         RWNRET:				 ; WM 4782
  06AF'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RWNREC -- DEVIATION 8: RDPREV on OUTFCB (DE), except that a record below
                                ;SAMREC is the source's own, never written to name.$$$: it is read from the
                                ;source through SRCFCB and cleaned as FILLBUF cleans it.  HL = where.
  06B2'                         RWNREC:
  06B2'   CD 08C0'              	CALL	RECDEC		; OUTPOS - 1
  06B5'   D8                    	RC
  06B6'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06B7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  06BA'   EB                    	XCHG
  06BB'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC
  06BE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; CY iff OUTPOS < SAMREC
  06C1'   EB                    	XCHG
  06C2'   D2 06DA'              	JNC	RWNOUT
  06C5'   22 0022*              	SHLD	SRCFCB+22H
  06C8'   E1                    	POP	H
  06C9'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCFCB
  06CC'   CD 0832'              	CALL	RDSEC
  06CF'   D8                    	RC
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-21


  06D0'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06D1'   CD 03F8'              	CALL	CLNSEC		; bit 7 off
  06D4'   E1                    	POP	H
  06D5'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  06D8'   B7                    	ORA	A
  06D9'   C9                    	RET
  06DA'   E1                    RWNOUT:	POP	H
  06DB'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,OUTFCB
  06DE'   C3 0832'              	JMP	RDSEC
                                
                                ;MARKGB -- WM 4886: UPDMARK only when HL points at GAPBEG (falls into UPDMARK).
  06E1'                         MARKGB:				; WM 4886
  06E1'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  06E2'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,GAPBEG
  06E5'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  06E8'   D1                    	POP	D
  06E9'   C0                    	RNZ
                                ;UPDMARK -- WM 4898: after an edit, move the record marks that say which
                                ;records must be written again.  Each mark only ever moves one way here:
                                ;  OUTREC (TXTBEG/output side) is LOWERED to OUTPOS + the whole records from
                                ;  TXTBEG to GAPBEG, when that is lower (stored on CMP16's carry).  UPDMARK
                                ;  never raises it; only PAGEOUT (POFRSH) does.
                                ;  SRCREC and BAKREC (GAPEND/input side) are RAISED to RECBASE less the whole
                                ;  records from GAPEND to TXTEND, when that is not lower (stored on no carry).
                                ;CMP16 sets carry when DE < HL.  (The comment here used to say the opposite
                                ;for both sides -- issue #37.)
  06EA'                         UPDMARK:			; WM 4898
  06EA'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  06EB'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  06EC'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  06ED'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  06EE'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  06F1'   CD 0751'              	CALL	PTRREC
  06F4'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  06F7'   19                    	DAD	D
  06F8'   EB                    	XCHG
  06F9'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SAMREC		; DEVIATION 8: the source holds the text only
  06FC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		;   up to the edit's record
  06FF'   D2 0707'              	JNC	UMKSAM
  0702'   EB                    	XCHG
  0703'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SAMREC
  0706'   EB                    	XCHG
  0707'                         UMKSAM:
  0707'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTREC
  070A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  070D'   EB                    	XCHG
  070E'   D2 0714'              	JNC	UMKGAP
  0711'   22 0000*              	SHLD	OUTREC
  0714'                         UMKGAP:				 ; WM 4914 -- update the GAPEND-side marks
  0714'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,GAPEND
  0717'   CD 0751'              	CALL	PTRREC
  071A'   CD 0740'              	CALL	RECBASE
  071D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  0720'   EB                    	XCHG
  0721'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRCREC
  0724'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-22


  0727'   EB                    	XCHG
  0728'   DA 072E'              	JC	UMKBAK
  072B'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRCREC
  072E'                         UMKBAK:				 ; WM 4926 -- lower BAKREC if needed
  072E'   EB                    	XCHG
  072F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKREC
  0732'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  0735'   EB                    	XCHG
  0736'   DA 073C'              	JC	UMKDON
  0739'   22 0000*              	SHLD	BAKREC
  073C'                         UMKDON:				 ; WM 4934
  073C'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  073D'   C3 0000*              	JMP	POPRET
                                
                                ;RECBASE -- WM 4939: disk record base for the buffer (BAKPOS - source_rec + 7FFF).
                                ;7EH is the source FCB's random-record word (FCB 005C + 22H).
  0740'                         RECBASE:			; WM 4939
  0740'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  0741'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKPOS
  0744'   EB                    	XCHG
  0745'   2A 007E               	LHLD	7EH
  0748'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD
  074B'   11 7FFF               	LXI	D,7FFFH
  074E'   19                    	DAD	D
  074F'   D1                    	POP	D
  0750'   C9                    	RET
                                
